Match a polar-coordinate region
Polar coordinates describe a point by its distance \(r\) from the origin and its angle \(\varphi\). A rectangle \([r_{\min},r_{\max}]\times[\varphi_{\min},\varphi_{\max}]\) in parameter space becomes an annular sector under \((r,\varphi)\mapsto(r\cos\varphi,r\sin\varphi)\). Matching the boundary makes the connection between algebraic bounds and the resulting planar region visible.
The blue target is an annular sector. Move the four sliders to match it with the orange outline. Radii are ordinary coordinates; the two angle sliders are multiples of \(\pi\) (for example, 0.5 means \(\pi/2\)). Only the slider values are assessed.


